WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.752 --> 00:00:04.121
[Translation Notes]

2
00:00:04.221 --> 00:00:07.763
Time: Sengoku Era (~1493 - 1598),
a time when Japan was divided...

3
00:00:07.863 --> 00:00:10.969
into many warring providences
each ruled by a feudal lord.

4
00:00:11.178 --> 00:00:16.183
Location: Akaike, a small and
poor providence by the sea.

5
00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:19.430
Other: Ming Dynasty/Ming,
refers to China...

6
00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:22.022
which was ruled by the Ming at the time.

7
00:00:54.096 --> 00:00:54.888
Shouan!

8
00:00:58.767 --> 00:00:59.643
Don't worry.

9
00:01:00.394 --> 00:01:02.437
If we've come this far,
we should be safe.

10
00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:03.856
Listen up Kotarou,

11
00:01:03.981 --> 00:01:05.537
You need to go on
alone from here on out.

12
00:01:05.637 --> 00:01:06.108
What?

13
00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:08.235
If something happens along the way,

14
00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:09.903
Sell this for a sen.

15
00:01:10.571 --> 00:01:11.709
What about you, Shouan! ?

16
00:01:11.809 --> 00:01:14.825
I need to check if everyone
at the temple is safe.

17
00:01:15.492 --> 00:01:16.451
In Akeike,

18
00:01:16.577 --> 00:01:18.537
Head for the Mangaku Temple in Shirato.

19
00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.581
Monk Zekkai will help you.

20
00:01:20.873 --> 00:01:21.290
But..!

21
00:01:21.415 --> 00:01:22.583
Hurry up and go!

22
00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:23.542
Hurry!

23
00:02:03.832 --> 00:02:06.168
Once we pass this mountain,
you'll reach our providence.

24
00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:12.382
The footing's bad, so from
here on out we'll go by foot.

25
00:02:29.399 --> 00:02:30.317
How about this?

26
00:02:30.692 --> 00:02:31.777
Got it!

27
00:02:31.902 --> 00:02:33.416
It's finally time to shine!

28
00:02:33.516 --> 00:02:34.313
Put me in too!

29
00:02:34.413 --> 00:02:35.614
Hope you don't lose it all!

30
00:02:35.864 --> 00:02:36.448
Idiot!

31
00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:40.827
You've drank to much,
you're red as rooster.

32
00:02:56.552 --> 00:02:57.461
Boss!

33
00:02:57.561 --> 00:02:58.387
We've got some prey!

34
00:03:23.453 --> 00:03:24.413
What's wro-

35
00:03:36.425 --> 00:03:37.509
Release the arrows!

36
00:03:50.564 --> 00:03:53.025
Doshi, Kamou, the crates!

37
00:04:06.455 --> 00:04:08.207
Keep shooting! Keep shooting!

38
00:04:24.431 --> 00:04:28.435
Against those numbers, Lord
Rarou alone is enough.

39
00:04:58.674 --> 00:04:59.591
Die!

40
00:05:15.941 --> 00:05:17.484
It hurts!

41
00:05:18.068 --> 00:05:19.069
It hurts!

42
00:05:20.571 --> 00:05:22.030
It hurts! It hurts!

43
00:05:23.615 --> 00:05:24.992
It hurts! !

44
00:05:52.519 --> 00:05:54.563
You bastard! ! ! !

45
00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:11.580
Both crates are safe.

46
00:06:17.419 --> 00:06:22.341
Is this the level of
swordsmen in this country?

47
00:06:30.182 --> 00:06:34.728
Akaike Providence

48
00:07:03.966 --> 00:07:05.008
Hey! !

49
00:07:05.759 --> 00:07:08.136
You shitty dog, get out!

50
00:07:09.346 --> 00:07:11.431
Shit! I'm gonna beat you to death!

51
00:07:11.974 --> 00:07:13.100
Wait! ! ! ! !

52
00:08:21.919 --> 00:08:22.836
Tobimaru,

53
00:08:23.045 --> 00:08:24.421
We're eating well tonight!

54
00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:31.345
Just wait a second.

55
00:08:42.147 --> 00:08:44.900
After we eat, we're
leaving this village, ok?

56
00:08:45.943 --> 00:08:46.652
...ok?

57
00:08:55.953 --> 00:08:56.954
Whose there? !

58
00:08:58.413 --> 00:09:01.250
Not anyone suspicious, don't worry.

59
00:09:01.416 --> 00:09:02.584
Get out!

60
00:09:06.922 --> 00:09:08.549
When you say 'get out',

61
00:09:09.466 --> 00:09:11.009
Does that means this is your

62
00:09:12.511 --> 00:09:13.470
home?

63
00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:15.931
That's right! This is our home!

64
00:09:16.306 --> 00:09:19.268
We've been here looong before you came!

65
00:09:20.602 --> 00:09:22.938
Well then I'll rent myself this space.

66
00:09:26.692 --> 00:09:28.068
Tobimaru, let's go!

67
00:09:33.699 --> 00:09:35.534
Is that a fish I smell?

68
00:09:35.659 --> 00:09:36.535
Tobimaru!

69
00:09:48.338 --> 00:09:50.591
I'm chilled to the bone.

70
00:09:50.716 --> 00:09:53.169
Give it an hour and it should calm down.

71
00:09:53.269 --> 00:09:55.429
It sure is cold.

72
00:09:55.554 --> 00:09:58.390
To think we'd be escorting these Ming.

73
00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.852
Even I have my limits.

74
00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:08.650
Letting strangers like that into the
castle, what could the lord be thinking?

75
00:10:08.859 --> 00:10:12.279
The lord must have some plan.

76
00:10:12.988 --> 00:10:14.448
Talking about strange,

77
00:10:14.573 --> 00:10:16.950
They're building something
over at the Shishine Fortress.

78
00:10:18.035 --> 00:10:18.702
Oh,

79
00:10:19.286 --> 00:10:22.539
You mean that old fortress
in the mountains?

80
00:10:22.956 --> 00:10:25.617
I hear they searched
the entire providence...

81
00:10:25.717 --> 00:10:27.836
and decided on the Shishine grounds.

82
00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:30.380
Probably something to
do with the foundation.

83
00:10:30.672 --> 00:10:35.427
I heard they rounded up all the local
workers and started barking orders.

84
00:10:37.095 --> 00:10:40.307
What are they doing
out in that old place?

85
00:10:40.516 --> 00:10:45.312
There's no way we could know
how people from Ming think.

86
00:10:56.907 --> 00:10:58.450
That's a nice smell.

87
00:10:58.784 --> 00:11:00.202
It's our fish.

88
00:11:00.702 --> 00:11:03.914
I'll let you know that I don't
have a single fish for you.

89
00:11:05.374 --> 00:11:08.669
You haven't been living
here all that long, right?

90
00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:13.131
That smoke's coming up is
the sign of an unused tree.

91
00:11:13.715 --> 00:11:15.509
It hadn't been dried out.

92
00:11:16.009 --> 00:11:17.177
You didn't need to do that!

93
00:11:18.929 --> 00:11:20.639
Be careful, it's hot.

94
00:11:31.149 --> 00:11:32.317
I'm eating it.

95
00:11:32.526 --> 00:11:33.569
Do what you like!

96
00:11:33.944 --> 00:11:35.612
I didn't say it to you.

97
00:11:37.656 --> 00:11:38.949
I said it to the dog.

98
00:11:59.052 --> 00:12:03.223
Oh Yes, I did see a young child run by.

99
00:12:03.682 --> 00:12:04.641
Was he alone?

100
00:12:05.184 --> 00:12:07.477
I think he had a dog was it?

101
00:12:08.061 --> 00:12:09.855
When did you see him?

102
00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:12.524
It might've been this morning...

103
00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:14.318
Where?

104
00:12:15.402 --> 00:12:19.156
I've been getting bad at
remembering things these days...

105
00:12:19.698 --> 00:12:21.909
No matter what, you have to remember!

106
00:12:22.117 --> 00:12:24.912
Even if you say that...

107
00:12:27.539 --> 00:12:28.790
You remembered? !

108
00:12:35.756 --> 00:12:39.968
Hmm...I didn't think there was
anyone living in that temple.

109
00:12:47.935 --> 00:12:49.228
Tobimaru, run!

110
00:13:06.703 --> 00:13:09.206
We are the lord's army.

111
00:13:13.126 --> 00:13:14.253
Don't interfere!

112
00:13:14.753 --> 00:13:17.756
Don't you think this is
a bit rough for a kid?

113
00:13:18.632 --> 00:13:19.591
Move!

114
00:13:22.177 --> 00:13:23.720
Bastard! !

115
00:13:23.846 --> 00:13:25.764
Did you not hear what I said? !

116
00:13:26.056 --> 00:13:26.849
Don't draw it.

117
00:13:27.683 --> 00:13:28.725
Watch what you say!

118
00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:53.250
Sorry, but I don't plan on getting
any further involved in this.

119
00:14:14.438 --> 00:14:15.272
Tobimaru!

120
00:15:03.904 --> 00:15:04.821
Tobimaru!

121
00:15:05.447 --> 00:15:06.281
Tobimaru.

122
00:15:09.284 --> 00:15:10.244
Seems like poison.

123
00:15:12.788 --> 00:15:14.540
It's not something an amateur can cure.

124
00:15:15.415 --> 00:15:17.251
Though if you take him to a doctor,

125
00:15:17.501 --> 00:15:18.932
Where's a doctor?

126
00:15:19.032 --> 00:15:20.295
Ask in the village.

127
00:15:21.463 --> 00:15:23.173
If I go back I'll be captured.

128
00:15:25.175 --> 00:15:27.386
Then you'll have to ride a
horse to the next village.

129
00:15:27.970 --> 00:15:29.463
I can't ride a horse.

130
00:15:29.563 --> 00:15:32.558
Well then good luck on nursing him.

131
00:15:33.809 --> 00:15:36.436
I guess the dead won't be needing this.

132
00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:38.097
You plan on leaving? !

133
00:15:38.197 --> 00:15:41.483
You think I could live long
in a violent place like this?

134
00:15:43.068 --> 00:15:44.570
It's your fault!

135
00:15:44.862 --> 00:15:47.531
Tobimaru's dying because of you!

136
00:15:47.865 --> 00:15:50.317
He saved your life and you're
going to leave him! ! ?

137
00:15:50.417 --> 00:15:51.451
Have you no shame!

138
00:15:51.827 --> 00:15:53.745
And I'm the one who saved you!

139
00:15:53.996 --> 00:15:55.122
We're even.

140
00:16:03.463 --> 00:16:05.507
If you plan on living alone,

141
00:16:05.799 --> 00:16:07.718
Then don't depend on others.

142
00:16:15.267 --> 00:16:16.476
Wait!

143
00:16:20.647 --> 00:16:22.274
A...a deal!

144
00:16:22.482 --> 00:16:24.226
If you save Tobimaru,

145
00:16:24.326 --> 00:16:28.155
And take us to the Mangaku Temple
in Shirato, I'll give you this!

146
00:16:28.572 --> 00:16:30.282
It's worth ten ryo! It's a gem.

147
00:16:30.657 --> 00:16:31.629
Ten ryo?

148
00:16:31.729 --> 00:16:34.077
That's right, it's a gem.

149
00:16:45.631 --> 00:16:47.132
Well it doesn't look cheap.

150
00:16:47.466 --> 00:16:48.592
Of course!

151
00:16:48.800 --> 00:16:51.762
I've never told a lie!

152
00:16:52.971 --> 00:16:54.473
You can't come any closer.

153
00:16:54.598 --> 00:16:57.643
It'd be trouble if you
ran when I gave it to you.

154
00:16:57.851 --> 00:16:59.811
If you take us, I'll give it to you.

155
00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:00.896
What will you do?

156
00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:02.731
Shirato, eh?

157
00:17:03.732 --> 00:17:05.330
It is a bit far...

158
00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:07.152
You don't want this gem?

159
00:17:09.738 --> 00:17:11.240
Well it is a gem...

160
00:17:12.824 --> 00:17:14.243
Don't you want it! ?

161
00:17:16.495 --> 00:17:18.205
Don't you want it! ?

162
00:17:18.539 --> 00:17:20.207
Don't you want it? !

163
00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:31.426
Is Tobimaru ok?

164
00:17:33.470 --> 00:17:34.888
Is the town far?

165
00:17:37.558 --> 00:17:40.269
Answer me! I'm the one who hired you!

166
00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:43.981
The dog's in pain, but
he's still breathing.

167
00:17:44.857 --> 00:17:46.733
It'll still be a while until the town.

168
00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:48.277
Hurry up!

169
00:17:48.527 --> 00:17:49.778
The horse is exhausted.

170
00:17:50.028 --> 00:17:54.992
Plus even if there's a doctor, we
don't know if he'll look at a dog.

171
00:17:58.287 --> 00:17:58.871
Hey,

172
00:17:59.246 --> 00:18:01.331
Why are you being chased?

173
00:18:01.707 --> 00:18:04.293
If I'm working for you, you
should be able to tell me.

174
00:18:05.627 --> 00:18:07.671
If Tobimaru dies, it's your fault!

175
00:18:07.921 --> 00:18:09.415
I won't give you the treasure!

176
00:18:09.515 --> 00:18:10.841
I'll never forgive you!

177
00:18:11.091 --> 00:18:12.718
I'll curse you until I'm dead!

178
00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:16.346
What a boss.

179
00:18:34.406 --> 00:18:37.242
He says to hire more workers
and hurry the construction.

180
00:18:37.701 --> 00:18:38.827
Understood.

181
00:18:39.286 --> 00:18:43.139
First they give gold for
the land and workers,

182
00:18:43.239 --> 00:18:46.668
and now a hundred ryo
for more workers...

183
00:18:46.835 --> 00:18:50.172
None of it seems to make any sense.

184
00:18:50.506 --> 00:18:54.510
I'm sure they have a reason to hurry,
but even if we ask they won't tell us.

185
00:18:56.553 --> 00:19:00.766
It's probably got something to
do with the kid they're chasing.

186
00:19:01.183 --> 00:19:06.104
Still, the more they keep it a
secret the more I want to know.

187
00:19:06.355 --> 00:19:07.439
Indeed.

188
00:19:07.856 --> 00:19:12.611
But when they're vessels of the Ming
Dynasty, it's tough to lay a hand.

189
00:19:19.201 --> 00:19:22.913
The horse needs to rest,
so you bring him over.

190
00:19:23.914 --> 00:19:26.041
You should've just
bought a Samurai horse.

191
00:19:26.708 --> 00:19:28.752
I just bought the best one.

192
00:19:29.419 --> 00:19:30.671
You bring him over!

193
00:19:31.338 --> 00:19:33.507
Don't forget the saddle.

194
00:19:34.132 --> 00:19:36.301
If you take to long you'll get lost.

195
00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:39.054
Shit!

196
00:19:45.352 --> 00:19:47.729
I've done what I can, but...

197
00:19:48.188 --> 00:19:51.316
I've never worked on an animal before.

198
00:19:58.740 --> 00:19:59.658
Tobimaru!

199
00:20:05.539 --> 00:20:06.874
Will he be ok?

200
00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:08.709
The wound isn't bad,

201
00:20:09.001 --> 00:20:10.711
But the poison got into his body.

202
00:20:11.461 --> 00:20:14.256
Anyhow, the doctor said to make sure
he drinks water and doesn't move.

203
00:20:14.756 --> 00:20:15.257
Water?

204
00:20:15.966 --> 00:20:17.384
It'll drive away the poison.

205
00:20:22.472 --> 00:20:23.098
Shit!

206
00:20:23.515 --> 00:20:25.517
It's not going to work
while he's paralyzed.

207
00:20:26.185 --> 00:20:27.436
Put Tobimaru down.

208
00:20:27.769 --> 00:20:28.896
I said put him down!

209
00:21:02.221 --> 00:21:04.056
Did anyone see anything?

210
00:21:04.181 --> 00:21:07.984
Unfortunately, the villager
who led them here...

211
00:21:08.084 --> 00:21:11.647
seperated from the group
before they entered.

212
00:21:11.855 --> 00:21:12.606
I see.

213
00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:32.709
What do you mean by this?

214
00:21:48.475 --> 00:21:50.269
Was there a festival tonight?

215
00:21:54.606 --> 00:21:59.486
If you want, you can stay in the back.
It's empty so it should be comfortable.

216
00:22:00.696 --> 00:22:01.814
Thanks.

217
00:22:01.914 --> 00:22:05.492
Well I've got your
money, so I don't mind.

218
00:22:05.742 --> 00:22:09.126
Oh yeah, there's an bath on
the cliff just a little...

219
00:22:09.226 --> 00:22:12.165
walk from here. Take a
dip if you feel like it.

220
00:22:39.443 --> 00:22:41.361
Looks like I overslept.

221
00:22:44.698 --> 00:22:47.659
How's the little dog?

222
00:22:53.749 --> 00:22:55.167
Where are you going! ?

223
00:22:55.626 --> 00:22:57.586
I'm going to get a saddle in town.

224
00:22:58.045 --> 00:23:00.881
Saying something like that, you
aren't planning on running are you?

225
00:23:02.174 --> 00:23:04.843
If did that I'd have done
all this work for free.

226
00:23:34.665 --> 00:23:37.376
Is that him? The blond haired monster?

227
00:23:37.960 --> 00:23:41.922
Yeah, I hear he's a guest and has been
going in and out of the lord's castle.

228
00:23:42.089 --> 00:23:45.251
And I hear his eyes are blue!

229
00:23:45.351 --> 00:23:46.760
Is that true?

230
00:23:47.135 --> 00:23:47.803
Yeah.

231
00:23:52.266 --> 00:23:57.145
I hear that blue eyed
guy has a lot of gold,

232
00:23:57.312 --> 00:24:00.858
Better not get too close
though, or he'll eat you!

233
00:24:01.191 --> 00:24:02.568
Ain't that right.

234
00:24:03.110 --> 00:24:04.611
Is this good?

235
00:24:06.363 --> 00:24:08.699
That's a saddle from Ooatari...

236
00:24:09.449 --> 00:24:12.494
I brought a bunch when I moved here.

237
00:24:12.995 --> 00:24:15.330
Who'd want to stay in
that ruined providence.

238
00:24:15.789 --> 00:24:16.707
Yeah...

239
00:24:17.124 --> 00:24:18.834
Don't let it bother you.

240
00:24:23.797 --> 00:24:27.092
Kingai and Doshi haven't returned
from the search yesterday.

241
00:24:27.885 --> 00:24:29.469
They probably found a lead.

242
00:24:29.928 --> 00:24:32.681
I doubt anything could have
happened to those two.

243
00:24:42.191 --> 00:24:44.588
Still, I never would
have thought finding...

244
00:24:44.688 --> 00:24:46.528
a child would take so much effort.

245
00:24:47.112 --> 00:24:49.865
Indeed, we only have four days left.

246
00:24:50.782 --> 00:24:52.701
Eventually he'll come
to the temple, but...

247
00:24:52.826 --> 00:24:56.872
If we miss this full moon, we'll have
to spend another year in this country.

248
00:24:58.081 --> 00:25:00.334
I'm tired of this country already.

249
00:25:02.211 --> 00:25:05.339
But since it's for the
senyaku, it can't be helped.

250
00:25:06.131 --> 00:25:07.341
Senyaku?

251
00:25:08.258 --> 00:25:10.886
It seems like one big joke to me.

252
00:25:11.553 --> 00:25:15.182
Do you not use our drug because
you don't believe in senyaku?

253
00:25:15.474 --> 00:25:16.975
That's not the problem.

254
00:25:17.267 --> 00:25:20.812
The drugs you guys take at least work.

255
00:25:21.396 --> 00:25:22.981
But senyaku...

256
00:25:23.607 --> 00:25:25.984
That's something that
even I cannot know.

257
00:25:26.777 --> 00:25:31.240
Wait, then why don't you use our drug?

258
00:25:32.199 --> 00:25:33.784
Because it's boring.

259
00:25:50.759 --> 00:25:52.135
What's wrong?

260
00:25:54.221 --> 00:25:56.431
I feel...like having a little fun.

261
00:27:15.010 --> 00:27:17.179
Why don't you draw?

262
00:27:18.263 --> 00:27:21.225
Is your blade a fake?

263
00:27:37.241 --> 00:27:38.242
Lord Rarou!

264
00:27:41.703 --> 00:27:42.913
What is it?

265
00:27:43.163 --> 00:27:45.082
Kingai and Doshi have been killed!

266
00:27:50.003 --> 00:27:52.089
...and it was just getting fun.

267
00:28:26.874 --> 00:28:28.250
You sure are late.

268
00:28:28.542 --> 00:28:29.251
Really?

269
00:28:29.918 --> 00:28:32.963
Sure you weren't looking to sell me out?

270
00:28:33.255 --> 00:28:35.883
Who'd buy a twisted kid like you?

271
00:28:36.383 --> 00:28:37.384
Don't play dumb!

272
00:28:38.802 --> 00:28:42.264
You were trying to find out why
I'm being chased, weren't you?

273
00:28:42.514 --> 00:28:45.309
I bet you were asking all around town!

274
00:28:45.517 --> 00:28:47.644
Brat, shut up already.

275
00:28:48.228 --> 00:28:50.105
I'm not 'brat', I'm Kotarou!

276
00:28:50.397 --> 00:28:51.899
What are you hiding from me? !

277
00:28:52.858 --> 00:28:55.861
Finding someone to sell me
a saddle took some time.

278
00:28:57.070 --> 00:28:59.114
That sounds like a big lie!

279
00:28:59.323 --> 00:29:00.908
What do I have to say
to make you believe me?

280
00:29:01.158 --> 00:29:03.368
Who trusts a man who works for money? !

281
00:29:03.577 --> 00:29:06.121
I hope you fall on your money!

282
00:29:07.664 --> 00:29:09.458
If you're going to go that far,

283
00:29:10.042 --> 00:29:11.376
Then should we part ways here?

284
00:29:11.752 --> 00:29:14.922
If you do that, you'll have done
all this work for free, right?

285
00:29:23.931 --> 00:29:24.890
Tobimaru!

286
00:29:25.098 --> 00:29:26.058
Tobimaru!

287
00:29:31.605 --> 00:29:33.057
Don't rush,

288
00:29:33.157 --> 00:29:34.733
Drink nice and slow.

289
00:29:40.489 --> 00:29:41.990
The doctor gave me this.

290
00:29:42.824 --> 00:29:45.661
'when he gets to the point where he
can drink water, he should drink this'

291
00:29:46.203 --> 00:29:48.789
He said it tastes real bad so
he'll probably give a fight.

292
00:29:50.624 --> 00:29:52.584
I'll make dinner.

293
00:29:58.924 --> 00:30:01.343
Wait, I'll help you drink it.

294
00:30:13.397 --> 00:30:17.109
The clothes and sword are
Doshi's, but it's someone else.

295
00:30:17.442 --> 00:30:20.863
Doshi had an old scar on his
right arm down to the bone.

296
00:30:21.321 --> 00:30:24.783
There was no scar on the burned corpse?

297
00:30:25.367 --> 00:30:28.328
There were also several
other things off.

298
00:30:28.871 --> 00:30:31.442
Going by the corpse
conditions, the first to die...

299
00:30:31.542 --> 00:30:33.959
were Kingai and two soldiers
of this providence.

300
00:30:34.293 --> 00:30:37.129
Kingai died by having his entire
neck shattered with a single blow.

301
00:30:37.421 --> 00:30:39.381
It must have been someone skilled.

302
00:30:39.715 --> 00:30:43.010
Looking at the wounds on the rest of
the corpses, it seems Doshi killed them.

303
00:30:43.260 --> 00:30:45.470
Kingai's hair was cut, but...

304
00:30:45.929 --> 00:30:48.724
I believe Doshi was the one who did it.

305
00:30:48.974 --> 00:30:53.145
Are you saying Doshi was attacked
by the soldiers of this providence?

306
00:30:53.395 --> 00:30:54.438
Likely.

307
00:30:55.105 --> 00:30:56.682
Then Doshi....

308
00:30:56.782 --> 00:31:01.236
Since they made it seem like he died,
it means he's likely alive somewhere.

309
00:31:03.530 --> 00:31:06.200
It's become troublesome, hasn't it?

310
00:31:30.682 --> 00:31:31.767
I'm sorry.

311
00:31:33.685 --> 00:31:35.687
I'm sorry...for before.

312
00:31:36.563 --> 00:31:38.649
I...lost my temper.

313
00:31:40.609 --> 00:31:42.528
We both did.

314
00:31:42.861 --> 00:31:44.530
Don't worry about it.

315
00:31:49.201 --> 00:31:51.370
I'm a little impatient,

316
00:31:51.578 --> 00:31:53.914
From now on don't make me wait too long.

317
00:32:30.742 --> 00:32:31.577
That's...?

318
00:32:31.743 --> 00:32:34.288
It sounds like it's
from the west wing...

319
00:32:34.580 --> 00:32:39.251
I heard the guests were trying out
a gift that was brought for them.

320
00:32:39.668 --> 00:32:40.961
A terrible sound...

321
00:32:42.087 --> 00:32:43.755
I sense an ill-omen.

322
00:32:53.307 --> 00:32:55.642
What kind of charm is that?

323
00:32:56.602 --> 00:32:58.979
It makes it so you can't
draw the sword, right?

324
00:33:02.566 --> 00:33:04.852
It's like a prayer type thing.

325
00:33:04.952 --> 00:33:06.520
What kind of prayer?

326
00:33:06.620 --> 00:33:08.405
It's a secret to others.

327
00:33:09.198 --> 00:33:11.408
Hmph, getting me all interested.

328
00:33:18.207 --> 00:33:18.916
Good, good.

329
00:33:19.249 --> 00:33:21.710
You're really nice to horses.

330
00:33:24.087 --> 00:33:27.508
What benefit is there to
having a horse in a good mood?

331
00:33:27.674 --> 00:33:29.051
There's lots.

332
00:33:29.551 --> 00:33:32.721
Like making him quiet so you
can sneak up and rob people?

333
00:33:33.055 --> 00:33:35.724
If you learn to ride a
horse you'll understand.

334
00:33:35.891 --> 00:33:38.101
If you ride a horse, you feel good.

335
00:33:38.769 --> 00:33:41.522
When you're on a horse
running at full speed,

336
00:33:41.730 --> 00:33:43.524
How do I say it...

337
00:33:43.815 --> 00:33:44.608
Yeah,

338
00:33:44.858 --> 00:33:47.027
It's like you're flying in the skies.

339
00:33:47.819 --> 00:33:48.695
The sky?

340
00:33:49.029 --> 00:33:51.323
That ain't a bad feeling.

341
00:33:52.908 --> 00:33:56.078
You feel a nice wind in your chest.

342
00:33:56.286 --> 00:33:57.538
And that's when you feel,

343
00:33:58.288 --> 00:34:01.166
Just a bit more free than you are now.

344
00:34:04.503 --> 00:34:05.546
Really?

345
00:34:10.509 --> 00:34:14.429
Does it really feel nice like
you're flying in the sky?

346
00:34:19.810 --> 00:34:23.230
Whether or not it does, that's something
for you to find out for yourself.

347
00:34:44.459 --> 00:34:45.669
Owww.

348
00:34:46.295 --> 00:34:47.767
It's because you're swaying.

349
00:34:47.867 --> 00:34:51.341
It's not my fault. It's
because this horse is rough!

350
00:34:51.633 --> 00:34:52.676
How's he rough?

351
00:34:52.843 --> 00:34:54.503
He's extremely calm.

352
00:34:54.603 --> 00:34:57.389
Look, he's been neutered.

353
00:34:58.974 --> 00:35:00.976
It's to make him calm.

354
00:35:01.560 --> 00:35:03.770
What do you want to do? Quit already?

355
00:35:26.293 --> 00:35:30.756
It didn't seem like they suspected us.

356
00:35:30.923 --> 00:35:32.395
Don't let your guard down.

357
00:35:32.495 --> 00:35:34.919
You've always been too cautious.

358
00:35:35.019 --> 00:35:36.053
What results do you have?

359
00:35:36.178 --> 00:35:38.847
I've never seen a man
with endurance like this.

360
00:35:38.972 --> 00:35:41.934
No matter how many times he's
burned he doesn't bat an eyebrow.

361
00:35:44.520 --> 00:35:45.979
Let me see.

362
00:35:55.739 --> 00:35:58.742
Oh! This is unbelievable!

363
00:35:59.409 --> 00:36:01.161
What do you think, Shougen?

364
00:36:01.286 --> 00:36:04.081
Even if we speak different
words, we're both human.

365
00:36:04.289 --> 00:36:09.670
To not feel pain. Even before
my eyes it seems unbelievable.

366
00:36:09.795 --> 00:36:13.715
Lord! Please leave the
interrogation to me.

367
00:36:14.091 --> 00:36:16.385
Yes, you are a dependable man.

368
00:36:16.635 --> 00:36:19.137
Itadori Shougen, I'm leaving it to you.

369
00:36:19.263 --> 00:36:24.184
Interrogate this Ming and make
some sort of deal with him.

370
00:36:28.146 --> 00:36:31.441
Oh Mr. Samurai, you sure are up early.

371
00:36:31.692 --> 00:36:32.580
You as well.

372
00:36:32.680 --> 00:36:36.613
I was thinking about going down to town.

373
00:36:36.738 --> 00:36:40.692
I've got these crops I'm
hoping to sell for a...

374
00:36:40.792 --> 00:36:44.830
fortune and then enjoy a
drink or two down there.

375
00:37:04.933 --> 00:37:06.977
Smells like cow shit!

376
00:37:07.477 --> 00:37:09.021
It's from the berries.

377
00:37:09.813 --> 00:37:12.024
If it cooks a little longer
the smell will go away.

378
00:37:12.649 --> 00:37:15.611
Are you trying to kill me so
you can steal the treasure?

379
00:37:17.362 --> 00:37:18.363
Seriously...

380
00:37:18.989 --> 00:37:21.158
A bad boss sure makes you work.

381
00:37:22.409 --> 00:37:24.737
I'll give you twenty mon for all of it.

382
00:37:24.837 --> 00:37:26.947
How about just a little bit more?

383
00:37:27.047 --> 00:37:28.540
No, no.

384
00:37:28.665 --> 00:37:31.710
If you don't like it, you
can try somewhere else.

385
00:37:41.553 --> 00:37:43.931
What's it say?

386
00:37:44.264 --> 00:37:47.935
The lord is looking
for a kid with a dog.

387
00:37:48.477 --> 00:37:51.939
There's a huge reward to
the one who finds him.

388
00:37:52.272 --> 00:37:54.483
A kid with a dog, eh?

389
00:37:54.650 --> 00:37:57.194
There are thousands
of those around here,

390
00:37:57.319 --> 00:37:59.404
Don't waste your time on this!

391
00:38:05.285 --> 00:38:05.827
Hey,

392
00:38:08.080 --> 00:38:10.791
These strangers think they can
just waltz around the castle.

393
00:38:14.002 --> 00:38:16.046
I...I've lost.

394
00:38:16.588 --> 00:38:19.508
You're still too weak to draw a bow.

395
00:38:19.842 --> 00:38:20.543
Next!

396
00:38:20.643 --> 00:38:21.718
Yes!

397
00:38:45.784 --> 00:38:48.662
Sorry about that, my hand
slipped from the sweat.

398
00:38:49.162 --> 00:38:52.207
How about it? Watching
must be a bore for you,

399
00:38:52.583 --> 00:38:54.251
Up for a match?

400
00:38:57.129 --> 00:38:58.581
Oh yeah...

401
00:38:58.681 --> 00:39:00.883
You don't understand
what I'm saying, eh?

402
00:39:01.300 --> 00:39:03.385
Well I guess we're in trouble here.

403
00:39:28.535 --> 00:39:29.953
Throw me a wooden sword!

404
00:39:43.217 --> 00:39:45.344
Excuse me,

405
00:39:48.597 --> 00:39:51.183
I guess they're...out?

406
00:39:54.144 --> 00:39:56.117
Thanks for the room.

407
00:39:56.217 --> 00:39:57.147
What's it say?

408
00:40:00.526 --> 00:40:04.404
If you're going to live alone, you
better learn to read and write.

409
00:40:04.530 --> 00:40:06.073
Your back's slumping.

410
00:40:06.782 --> 00:40:09.117
I didn't tell you to get all rigid.

411
00:40:09.743 --> 00:40:11.245
You don't need to bug
me about everything!

412
00:40:11.578 --> 00:40:14.915
If I don't tell you you're
awful, you'll never get good.

413
00:40:15.290 --> 00:40:17.876
If you just tell me what I'm
doing right, I'll get even better!

414
00:40:21.755 --> 00:40:23.382
The weather's so nice.

415
00:40:24.299 --> 00:40:26.677
To think that someone
actually injured you,

416
00:40:26.802 --> 00:40:28.929
Who was it you fought?

417
00:40:29.388 --> 00:40:31.431
A man from the Ming Dynasty.

418
00:40:31.682 --> 00:40:34.852
He had blue eyes, and
was over six feet tall!

419
00:40:35.143 --> 00:40:37.563
Wow, like a real demon.

420
00:40:37.729 --> 00:40:39.690
He might be scarier than a demon.

421
00:40:39.857 --> 00:40:43.068
He's the second person I've ever
seen with that level of skill.

422
00:40:43.485 --> 00:40:44.570
The second?

423
00:40:44.778 --> 00:40:46.572
An old acquaintance of mine.

424
00:40:46.989 --> 00:40:50.617
When I served the Ooatari Providence.

425
00:40:50.742 --> 00:40:54.037
We fought side by side in the wars,

426
00:40:54.288 --> 00:40:58.375
But after a certain
battle, he disappeared.

427
00:40:59.042 --> 00:41:01.141
Seems he'd gotten sick of war.

428
00:41:01.241 --> 00:41:03.630
Then he was a kind man, right?

429
00:41:04.339 --> 00:41:06.466
He was just weak hearted.

430
00:41:06.717 --> 00:41:11.597
He's a man that threw away
the god's gift that he had.

431
00:41:11.930 --> 00:41:16.643
So then how will you
use your gifted skills?

432
00:41:16.977 --> 00:41:21.523
That's easy. I'll use it to get even
more strength and climb even higher.

433
00:41:22.608 --> 00:41:25.235
You sound almost as if you're
going to conquer the country.

434
00:41:26.195 --> 00:41:30.741
I've got no intention of an
aspiration within a set height.

435
00:41:31.200 --> 00:41:36.288
Me, I'll set my height at
the peak of my aspiration!

436
00:41:48.550 --> 00:41:50.010
That's a lot of scars!

437
00:41:50.802 --> 00:41:53.347
They're what I got for going to war.

438
00:41:53.597 --> 00:41:55.807
What providence did you serve?

439
00:41:56.600 --> 00:41:58.227
It's not worth naming,

440
00:41:58.352 --> 00:42:01.355
It was destroyed and
doesn't exist anymore.

441
00:42:02.022 --> 00:42:03.732
You don't volunteer anymore?

442
00:42:06.318 --> 00:42:07.236
Yeah...

443
00:42:07.361 --> 00:42:08.779
I got sick of it.

444
00:42:12.324 --> 00:42:15.327
Oh yeah, I still haven't
asked you your name?

445
00:42:15.911 --> 00:42:19.665
As a samurai you must have
some really fancy name, right?

446
00:42:21.250 --> 00:42:22.000
Akage

447
00:42:22.334 --> 00:42:24.795
Yeah, that's a cool one.

448
00:42:25.420 --> 00:42:26.705
[Nanashi = Nameless]

449
00:42:26.805 --> 00:42:28.090
Akaomi Nanashi

450
00:42:28.340 --> 00:42:31.051
What! ? Don't tease me!

451
00:42:35.305 --> 00:42:36.515
I'm not teasing you.

452
00:42:37.558 --> 00:42:39.560
It's Nanashi because I've got no name.

453
00:42:40.352 --> 00:42:43.856
I've had quite a few names, having to
change it along with the providence.

454
00:42:57.244 --> 00:42:58.912
Grab that bamboo shute.

455
00:43:20.726 --> 00:43:22.686
By dying it with berries,

456
00:43:23.020 --> 00:43:25.022
It should last another ten days.

457
00:43:25.814 --> 00:43:28.150
You're a...foreigner?

458
00:43:28.525 --> 00:43:30.944
Who knows? Even I don't.

459
00:43:32.196 --> 00:43:34.698
I hear I was picked up
from a foreign ship,

460
00:43:35.073 --> 00:43:36.867
But I was the only one left alive.

461
00:43:38.493 --> 00:43:40.829
There were those that hated me,

462
00:43:40.954 --> 00:43:43.749
But since I learned this method,
those problems went away.

463
00:43:44.666 --> 00:43:48.378
The life I have now is far better
than the one I had as a general.

464
00:44:00.224 --> 00:44:01.391
What's wrong?

465
00:44:01.558 --> 00:44:03.936
If you stand there you'll catch a cold.

466
00:44:11.443 --> 00:44:13.278
You sure are quiet suddenly.

467
00:44:13.487 --> 00:44:15.739
Did my hair color scare you?

468
00:44:15.864 --> 00:44:17.491
I'm not scared at all!

469
00:44:17.616 --> 00:44:19.952
I've seen hundreds of foreigners before!

470
00:44:20.118 --> 00:44:22.913
It's just...I was surprised.

471
00:44:25.332 --> 00:44:26.875
You feeling good little dog?

472
00:44:28.877 --> 00:44:29.837
Pursuers.

473
00:44:30.546 --> 00:44:33.298
Pretend you haven't noticed and
start talking about something.

474
00:44:34.591 --> 00:44:35.438
What?

475
00:44:35.538 --> 00:44:38.971
Still, I'm surprised you've
seen so many foreigners.

476
00:44:39.555 --> 00:44:41.139
Where did you see them?

477
00:44:41.682 --> 00:44:42.933
Tell me.

478
00:44:46.895 --> 00:44:48.188
In the Ming Dynasty,

479
00:44:48.814 --> 00:44:51.191
Until two years ago,
that's where I lived.

480
00:44:51.692 --> 00:44:53.151
Were you living by yourself?

481
00:44:53.694 --> 00:44:55.904
I was with my little
brother and Tobimaru.

482
00:44:56.280 --> 00:44:57.406
And your mother?

483
00:44:58.365 --> 00:45:01.368
I hear she died soon after I was born.

484
00:45:01.827 --> 00:45:02.744
Your dad?

485
00:45:03.453 --> 00:45:06.832
When I was six...he left.

486
00:45:07.833 --> 00:45:10.377
With no parents, how'd you come here?

487
00:45:11.211 --> 00:45:13.714
One day, when I was about to be sold,

488
00:45:13.964 --> 00:45:16.967
A monk, who came to Ming
to train, saved me.

489
00:45:18.594 --> 00:45:21.305
And then he let me ride on
the bought back here with him.

490
00:45:21.597 --> 00:45:24.933
After reaching here I
lived at his temple.

491
00:45:26.059 --> 00:45:27.728
Why'd you leave the temple?

492
00:45:29.688 --> 00:45:30.689
The temple...

493
00:45:31.190 --> 00:45:32.816
was attacked.

494
00:45:42.284 --> 00:45:44.286
Let go! I said let go!

495
00:45:44.411 --> 00:45:45.654
From Akaike?

496
00:45:45.754 --> 00:45:48.498
No, no, no, no that's not it!

497
00:45:48.624 --> 00:45:52.294
We're just thieves passing by!

498
00:45:52.461 --> 00:45:54.213
Just thieves!

499
00:45:54.379 --> 00:45:56.340
Tobimaru, let him go.

500
00:45:58.258 --> 00:45:59.481
Please forgive me!

501
00:45:59.581 --> 00:46:01.637
Please forgive me! !

502
00:46:01.970 --> 00:46:03.472
Hurry up and get lost.

503
00:46:04.014 --> 00:46:06.058
Th...Thank you!

504
00:46:11.480 --> 00:46:12.731
Well then...

505
00:46:12.981 --> 00:46:14.233
Wait a second.

506
00:46:16.151 --> 00:46:18.320
Leave all your money.

507
00:46:19.071 --> 00:46:22.324
Money? No we don't even have a sen!

508
00:46:22.574 --> 00:46:23.992
Come on,

509
00:46:24.660 --> 00:46:27.871
Please believe me! If we had
money, we wouldn't be thieving!

510
00:46:30.457 --> 00:46:31.708
A nice sound.

511
00:46:43.595 --> 00:46:45.305
Silly thieves.

512
00:46:45.472 --> 00:46:47.015
Even silly people are good sometimes!

513
00:46:47.766 --> 00:46:50.185
I was planning on speeding up a bit,

514
00:46:50.686 --> 00:46:51.979
Is the dog ok?

515
00:46:52.104 --> 00:46:55.357
Yeah. If anythings wrong, I'll tell you.

516
00:46:56.024 --> 00:46:58.986
Hang on tight so you don't fall!

517
00:46:59.152 --> 00:47:00.070
Ok!

518
00:47:23.093 --> 00:47:26.096
Your right. It really
feels like we're flying.

519
00:47:26.430 --> 00:47:27.806
It's not bad at all!

520
00:47:35.772 --> 00:47:38.233
It's taken many years...

521
00:47:38.692 --> 00:47:41.570
To get Byakuran before us,

522
00:47:42.154 --> 00:47:44.781
When the source of
immortality is in his hands,

523
00:47:45.490 --> 00:47:49.369
The Emperor will be most pleased.

524
00:47:50.913 --> 00:47:54.333
Geshin and Suishin are heading to
the temple tonight as planned.

525
00:47:54.666 --> 00:47:58.212
Kachuu will be in charge of the
ritual at the alter tomorrow.

526
00:47:58.629 --> 00:48:00.968
Everyone else, either work
on finding the child,

527
00:48:01.068 --> 00:48:03.258
or the preparations for
escaping this castle.

528
00:48:03.550 --> 00:48:05.511
The alter finished in time,

529
00:48:05.802 --> 00:48:08.297
But the rest of the plan
has been a complete mess.

530
00:48:08.397 --> 00:48:11.308
I really could not face
the Emperor like this.

531
00:48:11.475 --> 00:48:13.989
I think it's about time
to start thinking...

532
00:48:14.089 --> 00:48:16.021
about if we do not have the child.

533
00:48:17.648 --> 00:48:21.527
If the full moon in two days passes,
the next won't be for another year.

534
00:48:21.902 --> 00:48:24.772
In that time it's possible
another war could break out,

535
00:48:24.872 --> 00:48:28.659
And this providence could be destroyed
causing us to lose everything.

536
00:48:28.784 --> 00:48:29.743
So then...

537
00:48:29.910 --> 00:48:33.038
If we delay the ceremony a
few days they'll never know.

538
00:48:33.247 --> 00:48:37.251
You're saying to send a
false message to the Emperor?

539
00:48:37.459 --> 00:48:40.087
I do not believe the blood will change.

540
00:48:40.212 --> 00:48:41.922
Shut your mouth!

541
00:48:42.047 --> 00:48:44.813
Or we find the child in Ming,

542
00:48:44.913 --> 00:48:47.678
And create an Alter in Ming.

543
00:48:47.803 --> 00:48:50.806
In Ming even if we have
to wait a year or two...

544
00:48:50.931 --> 00:48:52.558
That's enough!

545
00:48:59.022 --> 00:49:01.024
I'll go work on preparations for
our escape from this providence.

546
00:49:10.993 --> 00:49:12.035
That fool!

547
00:49:12.953 --> 00:49:16.331
To speak of fooling the Emperor!

548
00:49:16.748 --> 00:49:18.834
No matter how skilled he is,

549
00:49:18.959 --> 00:49:21.420
A warrior is just a warrior!

550
00:49:24.006 --> 00:49:26.758
There's no way to stop
you from handing him over?

551
00:49:27.342 --> 00:49:30.971
For the sake of our religion,
we can't refuse them.

552
00:49:31.138 --> 00:49:32.097
But...!

553
00:49:32.472 --> 00:49:33.778
This would defy our Buddhist ideals-

554
00:49:33.878 --> 00:49:34.884
You fool!

555
00:49:34.984 --> 00:49:37.803
Protecting our religion is our ideal!

556
00:49:37.903 --> 00:49:40.222
Be happy you are still alive!

557
00:49:40.322 --> 00:49:41.356
Wait!

558
00:49:41.940 --> 00:49:42.816
Let go!

559
00:49:58.040 --> 00:49:59.082
This voice...?

560
00:49:59.291 --> 00:50:01.418
It suddenly started two hours ago.

561
00:50:08.884 --> 00:50:11.649
So in the end you didn't get the reward?

562
00:50:11.749 --> 00:50:16.842
The Samurai thought I was lying to him.

563
00:50:16.942 --> 00:50:21.063
He was really really mad. I
thought I was going to die.

564
00:50:21.480 --> 00:50:24.358
I told you, you gotta stay away
from deals that sound too good.

565
00:50:29.613 --> 00:50:32.032
I wonder if it'll snow tomorrow?

566
00:50:32.157 --> 00:50:33.075
Huh?

567
00:50:33.700 --> 00:50:36.370
Look how sunny it is,
what are you saying?

568
00:50:36.537 --> 00:50:42.576
Look, even though the west sky is cloudy
I can see the sun shining all bright.

569
00:50:42.676 --> 00:50:45.796
That's a symbol that it's gonna snow.

570
00:50:47.923 --> 00:50:49.550
He's told us everything.

571
00:50:49.650 --> 00:50:50.050
Drug! Hurry! The Drug!

572
00:50:56.056 --> 00:50:56.974
This is?

573
00:50:57.349 --> 00:50:59.518
The drug he had on him.

574
00:51:00.853 --> 00:51:03.689
This is what he's like when
he can't depend on it?

575
00:51:03.814 --> 00:51:05.107
Put him to rest.

576
00:51:10.946 --> 00:51:12.322
Senyaku?

577
00:51:13.532 --> 00:51:15.693
According to the warrior we captured,

578
00:51:15.793 --> 00:51:20.831
They're searching for a drug
that makes one immortal.

579
00:51:21.665 --> 00:51:24.126
Immortal?

580
00:51:36.263 --> 00:51:40.029
It was foretold in a Ming prophecy.

581
00:51:40.129 --> 00:51:43.103
That was the start of it?

582
00:51:43.437 --> 00:51:44.479
Yes.

583
00:51:44.897 --> 00:51:48.859
According to the warrior Doshi,
it allows you to live forever.

584
00:51:49.568 --> 00:51:51.657
Once every hundred years
a child is foretold...

585
00:51:51.757 --> 00:51:53.572
of, and that by taking
the child's blood,

586
00:51:53.864 --> 00:51:56.408
You can create a drug
that makes you immortal.

587
00:51:57.242 --> 00:51:58.869
The Emperor believes this,

588
00:51:59.077 --> 00:52:01.246
And ordered his men to find the child.

589
00:52:01.371 --> 00:52:03.582
The pursuers crossed
the ocean to find him?

590
00:52:04.499 --> 00:52:07.377
The alter at the fortress, a
mechanism to engrave the time,

591
00:52:08.212 --> 00:52:12.424
This is all to gather the blood
according to the foretelling.

592
00:52:14.843 --> 00:52:17.429
Once every hundred years?

593
00:52:17.679 --> 00:52:21.558
Still...is immortality even possible?

594
00:52:22.142 --> 00:52:23.685
Who cares!

595
00:52:24.645 --> 00:52:29.858
What's important is that the child's
worth even more than a ship of gold.

596
00:52:30.192 --> 00:52:31.485
What should we do now?

597
00:52:31.818 --> 00:52:33.187
As if I need to tell you?

598
00:52:33.287 --> 00:52:37.491
Find the child first, and make
the foreigners disappear.

599
00:52:37.699 --> 00:52:42.037
But they're the only ones who
know what the child looks like...

600
00:52:42.329 --> 00:52:46.208
And since yesterday they've been
snooping around the whole providence.

601
00:52:46.458 --> 00:52:48.168
I've already taken a step.

602
00:52:48.377 --> 00:52:50.534
Even if they can't speak our language,

603
00:52:50.634 --> 00:52:52.965
I'll have them at
least crying in defeat.

604
00:52:53.507 --> 00:52:55.676
No matter what they try to do,

605
00:52:55.968 --> 00:52:58.220
This is our providence!

606
00:53:05.769 --> 00:53:08.021
Are you sad because Rarou isn't around?

607
00:53:09.398 --> 00:53:12.150
Almost like a wife whose
lost their husband.

608
00:53:12.526 --> 00:53:13.902
Don't make fun of me!

609
00:53:14.152 --> 00:53:17.690
The reason I look sad is because
I don't have my hawk at my side.

610
00:53:17.790 --> 00:53:19.408
Good job trying to hide it.

611
00:53:24.621 --> 00:53:27.541
If we fail tomorrow...another
year in this country?

612
00:53:28.959 --> 00:53:32.087
Still upset over your clash
with Lord Byakuran yesterday?

613
00:53:32.421 --> 00:53:33.172
That's nothing.

614
00:53:33.714 --> 00:53:38.385
What I'm thinking about is
the one who killed Kingai.

615
00:53:38.594 --> 00:53:39.887
Really,

616
00:53:40.512 --> 00:53:43.682
To care more about some tough
guy than the Emperor's orders...

617
00:53:44.516 --> 00:53:45.475
It's just like you.

618
00:53:45.809 --> 00:53:47.644
I'll follow the Emperor's orders.

619
00:53:48.270 --> 00:53:52.482
Even if that means ending
up like Doshi or worse.

620
00:53:53.734 --> 00:53:57.000
Right now the lord's army
is watching in wait,

621
00:53:57.100 --> 00:53:59.281
I'll be leading them.

622
00:53:59.531 --> 00:54:01.400
Make sure you keep up.

623
00:54:01.500 --> 00:54:02.868
I'll be looking forward to it.

624
00:54:16.340 --> 00:54:18.926
I wonder if that's the
princess playing...

625
00:54:21.595 --> 00:54:24.139
Give up on those aspirations.

626
00:54:24.765 --> 00:54:28.936
It's best to set your
aspirations within your limits.

627
00:54:33.065 --> 00:54:34.733
Wait up Lord Itadori!

628
00:55:14.439 --> 00:55:15.107
Hey,

629
00:55:17.025 --> 00:55:19.611
You're a pretty skilled
swordsman, aren't you?

630
00:55:20.821 --> 00:55:22.126
What about it?

631
00:55:22.226 --> 00:55:24.442
It would've been great if
you taught me, not just...

632
00:55:24.542 --> 00:55:26.410
how to ride a horse,
but how to sword fight.

633
00:55:28.704 --> 00:55:30.205
What'll you do if you learn how?

634
00:55:30.372 --> 00:55:33.500
What will I do? That's obvious,
it'll come in handy in life.

635
00:55:34.042 --> 00:55:36.628
The power of a sword's dependable!

636
00:55:37.546 --> 00:55:38.463
Depend on it...

637
00:55:39.756 --> 00:55:42.467
I thought like that when I was a kid.

638
00:55:42.926 --> 00:55:44.219
You think different now?

639
00:56:03.280 --> 00:56:05.490
You were really shook up.

640
00:56:07.117 --> 00:56:08.118
You've been awake?

641
00:56:12.748 --> 00:56:14.666
I can't sleep in this.

642
00:56:14.917 --> 00:56:16.293
I agree with that.

643
00:56:17.002 --> 00:56:20.881
Hey, you want me to teach you
a way to avoid bad dreams?

644
00:56:23.509 --> 00:56:27.721
You've just gotta hold something you
love and thing about nice things.

645
00:56:29.932 --> 00:56:32.851
That's what I've been
doing up until now.

646
00:56:51.119 --> 00:56:52.079
Lord Byakuran,

647
00:56:54.623 --> 00:56:56.333
Are you having trouble sleeping?

648
00:56:56.625 --> 00:56:59.586
I was thinking about something.

649
00:57:00.963 --> 00:57:02.047
Fuu,

650
00:57:02.256 --> 00:57:06.677
If you could live forever,
what would you do?

651
00:57:07.052 --> 00:57:08.262
Hmm...

652
00:57:08.512 --> 00:57:12.299
My desire is simply to live strongly,
even if it's for a short life.

653
00:57:12.399 --> 00:57:13.892
I can understand that.

654
00:57:14.184 --> 00:57:16.760
I've lived for so many
years now. It wouldn't...

655
00:57:16.860 --> 00:57:18.889
be strange for me to pass at any time.

656
00:57:18.989 --> 00:57:19.898
But,

657
00:57:20.065 --> 00:57:25.904
Strangely, the longer I continue to live
the greater my desire to live becomes.

658
00:57:26.196 --> 00:57:30.936
Even understanding that this
drug we search for by...

659
00:57:31.036 --> 00:57:35.414
the Emperor's order is
not to be used for myself,

660
00:57:35.831 --> 00:57:40.752
Somewhere deep down, I feel I'm
searching for my own benefit.

661
00:58:01.732 --> 00:58:04.860
To think Shirato's Mangaku
Temple was this amazing...

662
00:58:05.402 --> 00:58:06.820
The promised good.

663
00:58:10.449 --> 00:58:11.909
By the way,

664
00:58:12.117 --> 00:58:15.162
At the time I was all into
it and said it was a jewel,

665
00:58:15.579 --> 00:58:16.705
Actually...

666
00:58:16.830 --> 00:58:18.136
That's what I figured.

667
00:58:18.236 --> 00:58:18.665
Huh?

668
00:58:19.124 --> 00:58:21.418
It's the kind of thing you'd think of.

669
00:58:21.668 --> 00:58:25.714
Well, I should be able to at
least get about five ryo, right?

670
00:58:25.923 --> 00:58:27.007
Well....

671
00:58:29.176 --> 00:58:31.178
On....one ryo?

672
00:58:31.512 --> 00:58:34.014
Well it's not bad for a memento, right?

673
00:58:34.515 --> 00:58:35.974
I'm sure it's got its good points!

674
00:58:36.725 --> 00:58:38.977
What a kid.

675
00:58:39.102 --> 00:58:40.054
I'm not a kid, I'm...

676
00:58:40.154 --> 00:58:41.313
Kotarou?

677
00:58:44.149 --> 00:58:45.067
Kotarou!

678
00:58:45.943 --> 00:58:47.069
Shouan!

679
00:58:47.778 --> 00:58:49.071
Shouan!

680
00:58:52.783 --> 00:58:55.035
Shouan, you're safe!

681
00:58:55.452 --> 00:58:56.841
I was worried!

682
00:58:56.941 --> 00:58:59.498
I'm glad you're ok as well.

683
00:58:59.665 --> 00:59:00.999
I'm so happy,

684
00:59:01.124 --> 00:59:04.753
I thought maybe if I came here,
I'd be able to meet you again.

685
00:59:05.212 --> 00:59:06.296
I...

686
00:59:08.131 --> 00:59:11.468
Here, let me guide you
to monk Zekkai's room.

687
00:59:16.932 --> 00:59:18.183
Nanashi!

688
00:59:18.934 --> 00:59:20.519
See ya, kid!

689
00:59:21.812 --> 00:59:25.148
If you ever want a name, come
here and see me whenever!

690
00:59:25.816 --> 00:59:28.277
I'll think of an amazing name for you!

691
01:00:28.754 --> 01:00:29.713
Shouan?

692
01:00:32.090 --> 01:00:34.384
It took you quite some time to get here.

693
01:00:35.093 --> 01:00:37.012
Monk Zekkai?

694
01:00:38.055 --> 01:00:42.518
That was a long wait...we finally meet.

695
01:00:54.363 --> 01:00:55.418
Let me go!

696
01:00:55.518 --> 01:00:56.448
Let me go! !

697
01:00:56.698 --> 01:00:57.900
I said let me go!

698
01:00:58.000 --> 01:00:59.952
You tricked me, you bastard!

699
01:01:00.118 --> 01:01:01.245
I trusted you!

700
01:01:01.954 --> 01:01:03.163
Shit!

701
01:01:08.919 --> 01:01:10.337
Don't kill him.

702
01:01:10.504 --> 01:01:12.673
It'll be easier to
carry him if he's quiet.

703
01:01:13.048 --> 01:01:13.841
Let's go.

704
01:01:15.467 --> 01:01:17.761
They came. Get your swords ready.

705
01:01:18.136 --> 01:01:19.179
Attack!

706
01:01:22.516 --> 01:01:23.308
It's a trap.

707
01:01:39.324 --> 01:01:42.536
Run for the castle, we need
to inform Lord Itadori!

708
01:01:42.995 --> 01:01:43.996
Bastard! !

709
01:01:49.001 --> 01:01:50.002
So then,

710
01:01:50.627 --> 01:01:51.962
Where do you want to go?

711
01:02:07.186 --> 01:02:08.312
Hurry.

712
01:03:00.989 --> 01:03:01.949
Who are you! ?

713
01:03:03.116 --> 01:03:04.464
Where'd they take the kid? ! !

714
01:03:04.564 --> 01:03:05.381
Don't tell him!

715
01:03:05.481 --> 01:03:06.328
Don't say any--

716
01:03:07.079 --> 01:03:08.413
Answer me!

717
01:03:08.664 --> 01:03:10.040
Answer me!

718
01:03:10.374 --> 01:03:11.166
Tonight...

719
01:03:12.501 --> 01:03:15.921
Tonight...they plan on killing
him and taking his blood.

720
01:03:16.380 --> 01:03:17.748
For what purpose?

721
01:03:17.848 --> 01:03:18.603
I don't know.

722
01:03:18.703 --> 01:03:19.479
Where?

723
01:03:19.579 --> 01:03:20.133
I don't know.

724
01:03:20.342 --> 01:03:21.385
I just don't know!

725
01:03:21.593 --> 01:03:24.421
They didn't trust us.

726
01:03:24.521 --> 01:03:27.766
If we didn't hand him over,
they were going to kill us.

727
01:03:28.350 --> 01:03:31.144
You handed him over knowing
they were going to kill him? !

728
01:03:31.436 --> 01:03:33.730
I wanted to save him.

729
01:03:34.231 --> 01:03:35.899
It was monk Zekkai who decided it,

730
01:03:36.358 --> 01:03:37.393
Not me! !

731
01:03:37.493 --> 01:03:39.820
In the end you abandoned him!

732
01:03:44.408 --> 01:03:45.284
That's right...

733
01:03:46.118 --> 01:03:47.411
It's just as you say...

734
01:03:47.995 --> 01:03:51.081
Like you said, I abandoned that child.

735
01:03:51.999 --> 01:03:55.210
Being threatened...and
wanting to save my own life...

736
01:03:55.752 --> 01:03:57.171
I abandoned that child.

737
01:03:57.754 --> 01:03:58.672
But,

738
01:03:59.256 --> 01:04:01.091
If you had been in my place,

739
01:04:01.592 --> 01:04:03.677
You would've done the same as me! !

740
01:04:06.305 --> 01:04:07.306
Am I wrong?

741
01:04:07.723 --> 01:04:09.955
Can you even imagine
betraying your superiors...

742
01:04:10.055 --> 01:04:12.144
and following through
with your own ideals? !

743
01:04:12.811 --> 01:04:13.729
You can't!

744
01:04:13.854 --> 01:04:14.771
Right! ?

745
01:04:17.065 --> 01:04:18.692
Could you do it?

746
01:04:19.776 --> 01:04:21.332
You talk all superior,

747
01:04:21.432 --> 01:04:23.822
But are you going to save that child? !

748
01:04:24.031 --> 01:04:25.157
You won't.

749
01:04:25.324 --> 01:04:28.006
You won't go to something that
you know is certain death!

750
01:04:28.106 --> 01:04:29.161
You...

751
01:04:29.453 --> 01:04:30.746
In the end,

752
01:04:30.954 --> 01:04:32.372
You're the same as me!

753
01:04:51.642 --> 01:04:53.602
For a chicken shit like you,

754
01:04:54.228 --> 01:04:55.938
A monk's robe is a waste.

755
01:05:15.249 --> 01:05:16.458
What color?

756
01:05:16.792 --> 01:05:18.043
It's yellow and red.

757
01:05:19.044 --> 01:05:20.546
They got him in time!

758
01:05:20.796 --> 01:05:23.006
Yellow means they have the child,

759
01:05:23.173 --> 01:05:24.091
What's red?

760
01:05:24.258 --> 01:05:27.302
It means that this castle's
soldiers have betrayed us!

761
01:05:27.553 --> 01:05:29.638
Hurry and call Rarou.

762
01:05:36.270 --> 01:05:37.604
Please wait!

763
01:05:37.980 --> 01:05:38.897
Wait!

764
01:05:39.147 --> 01:05:40.691
I said wait!

765
01:05:41.525 --> 01:05:42.651
What business do you have here?

766
01:05:42.818 --> 01:05:45.153
I don't mind. Let him through.

767
01:05:46.405 --> 01:05:49.032
So you've noticed what really going on,

768
01:05:49.533 --> 01:05:53.245
So how will the deal go today?

769
01:06:24.776 --> 01:06:27.321
Why'd you attack without my order?

770
01:06:27.613 --> 01:06:30.691
The Lord's order was to get
the child as soon as possible.

771
01:06:30.791 --> 01:06:33.368
I'm the one in command of this army!

772
01:06:37.956 --> 01:06:38.928
Where's the child?

773
01:06:39.028 --> 01:06:40.834
It seems he doesn't know.

774
01:06:41.084 --> 01:06:42.669
I have a good guess where.

775
01:06:43.253 --> 01:06:45.088
It's likely the Shishine Fortress.

776
01:06:45.339 --> 01:06:47.549
What should we do with this monk?

777
01:06:47.883 --> 01:06:51.136
He's a traitor who conspired with
Ming. Send him to the other world.

778
01:06:51.303 --> 01:06:51.887
Yes sir.

779
01:06:52.221 --> 01:06:53.096
That's...?

780
01:06:54.765 --> 01:06:59.019
The monk's disciple. It seems he hung
himself while the other was unconscious.

781
01:06:59.853 --> 01:07:00.638
I see.

782
01:07:00.738 --> 01:07:02.523
For now, we're returning to the castle.

783
01:07:02.689 --> 01:07:05.400
The rest of you wait
here for the next order.

784
01:07:05.692 --> 01:07:07.236
A message!

785
01:07:10.072 --> 01:07:11.281
A message!

786
01:07:16.328 --> 01:07:17.217
The lord...?

787
01:07:17.317 --> 01:07:20.499
He was wide open with no guards!

788
01:07:21.041 --> 01:07:23.035
What about Isogai and Fuchiome?

789
01:07:23.135 --> 01:07:24.753
Unfortunately they were...

790
01:07:26.296 --> 01:07:29.132
You just sat and watched
the Lord be kidnapped?

791
01:07:29.258 --> 01:07:32.344
He said he'd kill me.
I couldn't do a thing!

792
01:07:32.594 --> 01:07:34.680
Why didn't you give chase? !

793
01:07:34.805 --> 01:07:36.682
The main horses were poisoned!

794
01:07:36.807 --> 01:07:38.892
All that was left were the work horses!

795
01:07:39.059 --> 01:07:41.854
We sent the Wataoki and Kawashi
armies towards the Fortress,

796
01:07:42.020 --> 01:07:45.566
But even if they rush, they
won't reach it before night!

797
01:07:46.108 --> 01:07:48.561
You sent the Wataoki and Kawashi armies?

798
01:07:48.661 --> 01:07:49.319
Yes sir.

799
01:07:49.528 --> 01:07:52.739
You are the only commander
left Lord Itadori!

800
01:07:52.865 --> 01:07:55.993
The princess said to
leave the command to you.

801
01:07:56.201 --> 01:07:57.953
I came as fast as I could.

802
01:07:59.955 --> 01:08:01.039
Jyuurouta,

803
01:08:01.373 --> 01:08:03.500
Get a horse and armor ready.

804
01:08:03.792 --> 01:08:05.752
One for each of us.

805
01:08:06.044 --> 01:08:06.920
Understood.

806
01:08:07.588 --> 01:08:08.964
We're changing plans.

807
01:08:09.089 --> 01:08:10.674
All of you, head for the castle.

808
01:08:10.799 --> 01:08:13.385
Myself and Jyurota will head
for the Shishine Fortress.

809
01:08:25.272 --> 01:08:30.819
While we buy time, Lord Byakuran
you cross over the sea.

810
01:08:31.111 --> 01:08:32.696
You sure gave us some trouble.

811
01:08:33.197 --> 01:08:35.324
Just a bit more patience.

812
01:08:35.532 --> 01:08:38.493
After we complete this, we'll
say goodbye to this country.

813
01:08:39.578 --> 01:08:40.829
That's true.

814
01:08:40.996 --> 01:08:42.748
We can finally go home.

815
01:08:50.005 --> 01:08:51.465
It's yours, right?

816
01:08:51.715 --> 01:08:55.052
The guy who chased us at
the Mangaku Temple had it.

817
01:08:55.719 --> 01:08:57.221
What happened to him?

818
01:08:57.721 --> 01:08:59.806
He should have been no
match for you, but...

819
01:09:01.683 --> 01:09:03.936
I sent him to the other world with this.

820
01:09:15.364 --> 01:09:17.574
Just because your masters not around,

821
01:09:17.699 --> 01:09:19.618
You better not bite me!

822
01:09:24.540 --> 01:09:25.582
Afraid?

823
01:09:28.377 --> 01:09:32.560
Pretending that you don't understand?
Or are you so afraid you can't speak?

824
01:09:32.660 --> 01:09:34.299
Everyone eventually dies.

825
01:09:34.675 --> 01:09:39.776
There's no one with infinite
time in this world.

826
01:09:39.876 --> 01:09:43.433
Even you'll live strongly in
the time that's left for you.

827
01:09:44.142 --> 01:09:45.602
If you're going to kill
me, hurry up and do it!

828
01:09:46.228 --> 01:09:49.898
Don't rush to your death, I
have something I must ask you.

829
01:09:50.232 --> 01:09:55.654
When you were taken from the temple,
there was a man who tried to save you.

830
01:09:55.988 --> 01:09:57.197
A friend?

831
01:09:57.364 --> 01:09:58.532
No idea.

832
01:09:58.866 --> 01:10:00.617
Answer honestly.

833
01:10:01.410 --> 01:10:03.537
I don't have any friends!

834
01:10:04.705 --> 01:10:07.916
It seems like I won't
get an answer from you.

835
01:10:08.375 --> 01:10:13.046
It doesn't matter...that man
was killed by my comrades.

836
01:10:27.603 --> 01:10:28.896
Jyuurouta!

837
01:10:29.062 --> 01:10:30.981
You know this area pretty well, right?

838
01:10:31.231 --> 01:10:34.151
There's a shortcut. But I don't
know if the horses can make it.

839
01:10:34.401 --> 01:10:36.195
I don't care if they break their legs,

840
01:10:36.320 --> 01:10:37.321
Hurry!

841
01:11:17.152 --> 01:11:18.403
Can you see it?

842
01:11:18.737 --> 01:11:22.962
When this hand points high,
your soul will leave your body,

843
01:11:23.062 --> 01:11:27.204
And the blood in your body will
continue to live for the Emperor.

844
01:11:28.121 --> 01:11:30.624
Think of it as an honor.

845
01:11:38.423 --> 01:11:39.842
Are you worried?

846
01:11:40.509 --> 01:11:41.301
No...

847
01:11:41.885 --> 01:11:43.087
Be not afraid,

848
01:11:43.187 --> 01:11:48.934
I hear Shougen is a great warrior,
with many comrades at his side.

849
01:11:49.059 --> 01:11:52.104
I am sure he will save the lord.

850
01:11:57.317 --> 01:11:58.373
Can you do it?

851
01:11:58.473 --> 01:12:02.544
The Wataoki and Kawashi armies
are like brothers to me,

852
01:12:02.644 --> 01:12:04.533
You won't need to worry.

853
01:12:04.741 --> 01:12:05.742
I'm counting on you!

854
01:12:05.868 --> 01:12:07.077
Leave it to me!

855
01:12:20.966 --> 01:12:22.050
It's Jyuurouta!

856
01:12:22.259 --> 01:12:24.761
Look! Lord Itadori has come too!

857
01:12:25.012 --> 01:12:26.346
Lord Itadori!

858
01:12:26.471 --> 01:12:28.182
We've been waiting for you!

859
01:12:52.623 --> 01:12:54.333
What should we do?

860
01:12:54.458 --> 01:12:57.336
Use the feudal lord as a
shield and buy us time.

861
01:12:57.961 --> 01:13:01.089
There's only two hours
left until the ritual.

862
01:13:16.271 --> 01:13:17.577
Th...the lord?

863
01:13:17.677 --> 01:13:18.941
What a disgrace.

864
01:13:20.359 --> 01:13:21.693
Shougen!

865
01:13:22.152 --> 01:13:24.626
Is that you Shougen?

866
01:13:24.726 --> 01:13:26.114
How can we attack now?

867
01:13:26.323 --> 01:13:29.493
What does Lord Itadori plan to do?

868
01:13:29.868 --> 01:13:30.911
Jyuurouta.

869
01:13:42.089 --> 01:13:43.340
Shougen!

870
01:13:46.718 --> 01:13:48.136
Don't panic!

871
01:13:48.762 --> 01:13:52.683
It's time for you to ask your hearts!

872
01:13:52.850 --> 01:13:54.176
Will you follow me? !

873
01:13:54.276 --> 01:13:56.311
Or will you follow the dead lord? !

874
01:13:56.979 --> 01:13:59.661
If you follow me, the
country is as good as ours!

875
01:13:59.761 --> 01:14:01.483
Bastard!

876
01:14:04.069 --> 01:14:06.572
I will follow Lord Itadori!

877
01:14:06.738 --> 01:14:08.031
What will you do? !

878
01:14:08.240 --> 01:14:10.158
I'll follow Lord Itadori too!

879
01:14:10.284 --> 01:14:11.869
Me...me, too!

880
01:14:12.327 --> 01:14:13.829
I'll follow Lord Itadori!

881
01:14:14.288 --> 01:14:14.788
Me too!

882
01:14:14.997 --> 01:14:16.081
Me too!

883
01:14:16.957 --> 01:14:19.501
We shall conquer this fortress!

884
01:14:22.838 --> 01:14:23.505
What?

885
01:14:23.797 --> 01:14:26.584
Unlike our Emperor,

886
01:14:26.684 --> 01:14:30.179
To them a lord is just a
descendant of a bloodline.

887
01:14:30.554 --> 01:14:33.015
Useless as a hostage it seems.

888
01:14:34.391 --> 01:14:36.268
Damn barbarians!

889
01:14:36.810 --> 01:14:38.979
I'm leaving the ritual up to Kachuu.

890
01:14:39.104 --> 01:14:41.106
Get down there and fight them off!

891
01:14:46.445 --> 01:14:47.613
Fire!

892
01:15:12.596 --> 01:15:13.138
Shit.

893
01:15:16.391 --> 01:15:17.476
Damn.

894
01:15:45.087 --> 01:15:46.129
Back!

895
01:15:47.464 --> 01:15:48.382
Forward!

896
01:15:54.763 --> 01:15:55.556
Forward!

897
01:16:05.065 --> 01:16:06.233
I'll be going first.

898
01:16:07.693 --> 01:16:08.873
Charge!

899
01:16:08.973 --> 01:16:10.237
Lord Itadori!

900
01:16:10.362 --> 01:16:12.322
After we've taken their heads,

901
01:16:12.489 --> 01:16:14.533
I have a request!

902
01:16:14.741 --> 01:16:16.910
You can have the princess to yourself!

903
01:16:50.527 --> 01:16:51.570
Got you!

904
01:17:04.208 --> 01:17:05.083
Bitch!

905
01:17:07.920 --> 01:17:09.213
That's what you deserve!

906
01:17:22.809 --> 01:17:23.894
Bows!

907
01:17:33.111 --> 01:17:34.530
Aim well!

908
01:17:40.911 --> 01:17:41.966
Split into two groups!

909
01:17:42.066 --> 01:17:42.454
Yes!

910
01:18:21.577 --> 01:18:22.911
Don't back down!

911
01:19:05.787 --> 01:19:07.039
Now's the time!

912
01:19:07.206 --> 01:19:09.499
Rush in while they're distracted!

913
01:19:17.174 --> 01:19:18.342
Back down!

914
01:19:18.467 --> 01:19:20.844
You guys go fight someone else.

915
01:19:21.845 --> 01:19:23.722
This guy's my...

916
01:19:23.931 --> 01:19:25.015
Prey!

917
01:19:25.766 --> 01:19:26.808
I wouldn't try.

918
01:19:27.392 --> 01:19:30.020
The spear is actually my true weapon.

919
01:19:30.270 --> 01:19:32.272
It won't go like before!

920
01:19:38.654 --> 01:19:40.697
I'm enough of an
opponent for all of you!

921
01:20:23.949 --> 01:20:27.077
I can't say I don't understand
where you're coming from,

922
01:20:27.619 --> 01:20:29.162
But it's an uneeded emotion.

923
01:20:29.997 --> 01:20:31.874
This is the world we live in.

924
01:20:32.416 --> 01:20:36.461
Our battle sounded the victory horn
for our lord to become the new ruler.

925
01:20:37.546 --> 01:20:40.340
This is all thanks to your hard work.

926
01:20:41.466 --> 01:20:42.426
In all honesty,

927
01:20:42.593 --> 01:20:44.595
I'm completely jealous.

928
01:21:15.375 --> 01:21:17.961
Hurry up and do it, you coward! ! !

929
01:22:33.620 --> 01:22:34.580
It's time.

930
01:22:41.545 --> 01:22:42.462
Tobimaru!

931
01:22:47.259 --> 01:22:48.635
Kotarou! ! !

932
01:23:02.733 --> 01:23:04.693
That guy...

933
01:23:08.363 --> 01:23:09.198
Move!

934
01:23:13.035 --> 01:23:14.244
Move! ! !

935
01:23:34.181 --> 01:23:35.015
Tobimaru!

936
01:24:39.538 --> 01:24:41.832
What's wrong? Come on!

937
01:24:42.791 --> 01:24:45.085
I'm not feeling any pain!

938
01:24:45.836 --> 01:24:49.715
Try to stab that sword through my heart!

939
01:24:50.549 --> 01:24:51.800
Come on! !

940
01:24:56.263 --> 01:24:59.057
Hurry up and get back
here! Kachuu's dead!

941
01:25:00.100 --> 01:25:01.768
I've taken care of the rest of them!

942
01:25:13.238 --> 01:25:13.947
Tobimaru!

943
01:25:20.913 --> 01:25:21.580
Let's go!

944
01:25:23.624 --> 01:25:26.431
The ritual's been
interrupted by someone!

945
01:25:26.531 --> 01:25:30.172
The time has passed.
What do you plan to do?

946
01:25:30.339 --> 01:25:31.519
Isn't that obvious? !

947
01:25:31.619 --> 01:25:32.666
We'll take back the child,

948
01:25:32.766 --> 01:25:35.461
And we'll wait. Whether it's
ten or a hundred years!

949
01:25:35.561 --> 01:25:36.512
Leave it to me!

950
01:25:46.438 --> 01:25:47.773
Seriously...

951
01:25:48.440 --> 01:25:50.025
This isn't going to be cheap.

952
01:25:52.486 --> 01:25:53.695
I knew it!

953
01:25:54.279 --> 01:25:55.614
I heard you!

954
01:25:55.948 --> 01:25:57.866
You called my name, right?

955
01:25:59.826 --> 01:26:01.912
Damn it, you're late!

956
01:26:02.704 --> 01:26:05.082
I told you I had a short patience!

957
01:26:05.582 --> 01:26:07.042
Making me wait like that...

958
01:26:08.585 --> 01:26:10.963
Alright, let's go. Don't fall behind.

959
01:26:12.297 --> 01:26:13.290
I know.

960
01:26:13.390 --> 01:26:15.259
I didn't say it to you.

961
01:26:16.510 --> 01:26:18.220
I said it to Tobimaru.

962
01:26:23.767 --> 01:26:24.810
Get back!

963
01:26:55.340 --> 01:26:56.300
Nanashi!

964
01:27:24.536 --> 01:27:25.787
Where's my sword? !

965
01:27:28.457 --> 01:27:29.750
Where's my sword?

966
01:27:32.628 --> 01:27:33.504
Nanashi!

967
01:27:42.804 --> 01:27:44.640
Lord Rarou...

968
01:27:46.308 --> 01:27:47.267
My...sword...

969
01:27:47.601 --> 01:27:48.852
Lord....Ra...rou...

970
01:27:53.649 --> 01:27:56.109
To kill Fuu and Suishin,

971
01:27:56.276 --> 01:27:57.811
An impressive man.

972
01:27:57.911 --> 01:27:58.862
Rarou!

973
01:27:59.571 --> 01:28:01.240
You're in the way. Move!

974
01:28:05.369 --> 01:28:06.203
Shit!

975
01:28:14.336 --> 01:28:15.671
This is the end for you!

976
01:28:27.224 --> 01:28:28.433
You bastard!

977
01:28:28.600 --> 01:28:30.803
Have you gone crazy? ! !

978
01:28:30.903 --> 01:28:32.062
I am very sane.

979
01:28:32.187 --> 01:28:34.773
I am now glad I came to this country.

980
01:28:35.774 --> 01:28:38.735
I feel I've finally found an
opponent who will challenge me.

981
01:28:40.904 --> 01:28:44.032
I thank you for taking
me on this journey.

982
01:28:44.199 --> 01:28:45.367
You...!

983
01:28:45.576 --> 01:28:47.661
Bastard warrior!

984
01:28:54.001 --> 01:28:55.286
Rarou!

985
01:28:55.386 --> 01:28:58.881
Planning to trick the Emperor
and keep the drug for yourself,

986
01:28:59.256 --> 01:29:01.083
You've thought this out well.

987
01:29:01.183 --> 01:29:05.546
You are not worthy of
immortality, you warrior!

988
01:29:05.646 --> 01:29:10.142
The one who is worthy is a
genius leader such as myself...

989
01:29:12.144 --> 01:29:14.062
Haven't you already lived plenty?

990
01:29:29.578 --> 01:29:30.871
What's happening?

991
01:29:30.996 --> 01:29:32.998
The foreigner killed his comrade.

992
01:29:33.457 --> 01:29:35.501
There's only...one left!

993
01:30:06.698 --> 01:30:08.158
We met before.

994
01:30:09.409 --> 01:30:10.285
Nanashi!

995
01:30:11.787 --> 01:30:12.538
Use this....

996
01:30:14.414 --> 01:30:15.582
USE

997
01:30:16.041 --> 01:30:16.917
DRUG

998
01:30:17.334 --> 01:30:18.252
PAIN

999
01:30:18.460 --> 01:30:19.461
GO AWAY

1000
01:30:25.759 --> 01:30:26.760
I don't need it.

1001
01:30:28.720 --> 01:30:32.474
I feel like having the pain
is what makes you feel alive.

1002
01:30:36.353 --> 01:30:37.575
That's great.

1003
01:30:37.675 --> 01:30:38.897
That's really great.

1004
01:30:39.898 --> 01:30:43.110
I like you more and more.

1005
01:33:56.386 --> 01:33:57.387
Nanashi!

1006
01:34:52.067 --> 01:34:55.445
This is the first time
I've ever been cut.

1007
01:34:55.737 --> 01:34:58.240
The pain of a sword,

1008
01:34:58.532 --> 01:35:02.286
Somehow...strange...

1009
01:35:02.786 --> 01:35:04.872
Strange...

1010
01:35:07.833 --> 01:35:11.753
A strange feeling...

1011
01:36:11.230 --> 01:36:12.898
You've gotten pretty good.

1012
01:36:13.607 --> 01:36:16.735
Somehow...I feel like
I'm walking on clouds.

1013
01:36:17.277 --> 01:36:18.654
You don't have to flatter me.

1014
01:36:19.780 --> 01:36:21.490
Are your wounds ok?

1015
01:36:21.865 --> 01:36:22.741
Yeah.

1016
01:36:23.033 --> 01:36:25.611
Even a treasure like that came in handy.

1017
01:36:25.711 --> 01:36:26.578
See?

1018
01:36:26.912 --> 01:36:27.746
Seriously...

1019
01:36:28.622 --> 01:36:30.707
What a boss.

1020
01:36:38.215 --> 01:36:40.509
Can you see the town yet?

1021
01:36:41.134 --> 01:36:42.427
Not yet,

1022
01:36:42.803 --> 01:36:45.305
I'm sure we're almost there!

1023
01:36:46.515 --> 01:36:47.224
Hey...?

1024
01:36:47.683 --> 01:36:48.350
Hey?

1025
01:36:49.226 --> 01:36:52.771
After you get better, how about we
cross the sea and leave this country?

1026
01:36:53.397 --> 01:36:55.456
In foreign countries there
won't be anyone who...

1027
01:36:55.556 --> 01:36:57.442
will bother you about
your hair color, right?

1028
01:36:58.277 --> 01:36:59.361
A foreign country...

1029
01:37:00.153 --> 01:37:02.314
That doesn't sound all bad.

1030
01:37:02.414 --> 01:37:03.740
How will we save up the money?

1031
01:37:04.032 --> 01:37:08.161
We can be bodyguards, or
thieves, or anything.

1032
01:37:08.328 --> 01:37:10.664
We can even start a pirate crew!

1033
01:37:11.206 --> 01:37:12.207
Man,

1034
01:37:12.958 --> 01:37:15.586
You're just looking for trouble.

1035
01:37:17.296 --> 01:37:18.539
I'm going to speed up a bit,

1036
01:37:18.639 --> 01:37:19.965
Hang on tight!

1037
01:37:21.967 --> 01:37:22.718
Alright.

1038
01:37:28.515 --> 01:37:29.641
Let's go!
